<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Falange Española de las JONS</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1934">1934</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FE de las JONS, Falange Española de las Juntas de Ofensiva Nacional Sindicalista, Falange</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Falange Española de las JONS was a national syndicalist political party founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1934 by the merger of the Falange Española with the Juntas de Ofensiva Nacional-Sindicalista of Onésimo Redondo and Ramiro Ledesma. Led from October 1934 by José Antonio Primo de Rivera as Jefe Nacional, it set out its programme in the Twenty-Seven Points, and in street violence with the Socialists it formed its own death squads. It won only 0.11% of the votes in the 1936 election. Primo de Rivera was executed in a Republican prison on 20 November 1936, and on 19 April 1937 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Francisco Franco</a> merged the party with the Carlists into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fet-y-de-las-jons">FET y de las JONS</a>, the sole legal party of his regime.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;Cara al Sol&quot; (&quot;Facing the Sun&quot;) is the anthem of the <b>Falange Española de las JONS</b>, the Falangist party of the Spanish far right.</blockquote><a href="/songs/cara-al-sol">Cara al Sol</a></li></ul></section>
